poulos A, Sexton PM, et al. Functional selectivity and classical concepts of quantitative pharmacology. J Pharmacol Exp Ther. 2007;320:1–13. doi: 10.1124/jpet.106.104463. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] [9]. Kenakin T, Christopoulos A. Signalling bias in new drug discovery: detection, quantification and therapeutic impact. Nat Rev Drug Discov. 2013;12:205–216. doi: 10.1038/nrd3954. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] ** [10]. Wacker D, Wang C, Katritch V, Han GW, Huang XP, Vardy E, McCorvy JD, Jiang Y, Chu M, Siu FY, et al. Structural features for functional selectivity at serotonin receptors. Science. 2013;340:615–619. doi: 10.1126/science.1232808..** Wacker D et al. have generated a high resolution crystal structure of the 5HT2B receptor bound to the biaised agonist Ergotamine. By comparing with the structure of the 5HT1B, they highlight molecular determinant regulating bias activity of the 5HT2B by Ergotamine. ** [11]. Wang C, Jiang Y, Ma J, Wu H, Wacker D, Katritch V, Han GW, Liu W, Huang XP, Vardy E, et al. Structural basis for molecular recognition at serotonin receptors. Science. 2013;340:610–614. doi: 10.1126/science.1232807..** Wang C et al. have generated a high resolution crystal structure of the 5HT1B receptor bound to Ergoatamine and dihydroergotamine. With the structure of the 5HT2B, they reveal important determinat regulating ligand specificity. [12]. Ostrom RS, Insel PA. The evolving role of lipid rafts and caveolae in G protein-coupled receptor signaling: implications for molecular pharmacology. Br J Pharmacol. 2004;143:235–245. doi: 10.1038/sj.bjp.0705930. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] [13]. Hakak Y, Shrestha D, Goegel MC, Behan DP, Chalmers DT. Global analysis of G-protein-coupled receptor signaling in human tissues. FEBS Lett. 2003;550:11–17. doi: 10.1016/s0014-5793(03)00762-2. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] [14]. Baker JG, Hill SJ. Multiple GPCR conformations and signalling pathways: implications for a