ers that occurred with wood block enrichment. Table 8. Experiment 1: Gene ontology processes modulated by wood block enrichment Tissue Modulation Biologic process P No. changed/ no. in pathway Liver Upregulated Anatomic structure morphogenesis 2.00E–05 2/6 Negative regulation of ERK1 and ERK2 cascade 1.29E–03 1/1 Lauric acid metabolic process 2.57E–03 1/2 Regulation of MAP kinase activity 3.85E–03 1/3 Regulation of glycogen catabolic process 3.85E–03 1/3 Asparagine catabolic process via L–aspartate 3.85E–03 1/3 Oxidation reduction 4.07E–03 3/250 Regulation of glycogen biosynthetic process 5.14E–03 1/4 Regulation of cell–matrix adhesion 6.41E–03 1/5 Cilium assembly 7.69E–03 1/6 Regulation of gene–specific transcription from RNA polymerase II promoter 7.69E–03 1/6 Programmed cell death 8.97E–03 1/7 Epithelial cell development 1.15E–02 1/9 Inactivation of MAPK activity 1.28E–02 1/10 Cell development 1.41E–02 1/11 Downregulated Nucleolar fragmentation 8.70E–04 1/1 Regulation of bile acid biosynthetic process 8.70E–04 1/1 Cellular response to cholesterol 8.70E–04 1/1 Cellular response to glucose stimulus 1.74E–03 1/2 Reentry into mitotic cell cycle 4.33E–03 1/5 Cellular sodium ion homeostasis 4.33E–03 1/5 Response to folic acid 5.20E–03 1/6 Cholesterol catabolic process 6.06E–03 1/7 Bile acid biosynthetic process 7.79E–03 1/9 Cellular response to starvation 1.04E–02 1/12 Protein import into nucleus, translocation 1.72E–02 1/20 Positive regulation of insulin secretion 1.81E–02 1/21 Negative regulation of transcription from RNA polymerase II promoter 1.85E–02 2/241 Cholesterol homeostasis 2.32E–02 1/27 Steroid metabolic process 3.84E–02 1/45 Spleen Upregulated Insulin–like growth factor binding 2.96E–03 1/23 Regulation of cell growth 9.10E–03 1/71 Extracellular region 1.28E–01 1/1047 Downregulated GTP catabolic process 6.00E–05 2/4 Neutral amino acid transport 2.30E–04 2/7 Porphyrin biosynthetic process 2.30E–04 2/7 Response to organic substance 2.30E–04 4/90 Cellular resp