INSERT INTO corpus VALUES(4700,'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8940586','Traditional Uses, Phytochemistry, Pharmacology and Toxicology of Rhizoma phragmitis: A Narrative Review.','Ren Y, Cui GD, He LS, Yao H, Zi CY, Gao YX.','2022','phragmitis quench disinhibiting weijing wuye lugen phragmitis phragmitis antioxidative botany phragmitis appendixes s11655 phragmitis 11655_2022_3572_moesm1_esm phragmitis 11655_2022_3572_moesm2_esm phragmitis 11655_2022_3572_moesm3_esm phragmitis proofreading sauvetre endophytic phragmites australis fpls langenhoff aam phragmites australis phytodegradation 7b00458 debus herbicides phragmites australis naturforsch znc phragmitis s10753 coumaric phragmitis phragmites australis liaoning rmf hauck biorefining arundo donax cortaderia selloana phragmites australis pretreatments fpls phragmitis comb rhizomas phragmites communis phragmitis kudiezi shenyang shenyang univisity hyperlipidemic phragmites communis phragmitis cheminformatics phragmitis liposoluble phragmitis shenyang phragmitis phragmites australis trin steud moschamindole mia40 intermembrane phytother ptr grigor galyautdinov khalilov indol coumaramide phragmites australis compd chlorella phragmites australis dalian dalian phragmitis aparicio agave tequilana pristane molecules22060848 phragmites macromol ijbiomac phragmites jmf phragmites communis oligosaccharides phragmites carbohydr polym carbpol phragmites australis metabolisms phragmitis glucolipid pharmacogn mazumder sumi golder aerial phragmites karka retz ehanol phragmitis kabir uddin mmn ethnopharmacological aerial phragmites karka poaceae jbcpp liaqat asghar methanolic phragmites karka tetrachloride hepatoprotective phragmites australis naturforsch phragmitis cjcmm phragmitis oxalate phragmitis phragmites nga barua moisturizing phragmites communis s12272 phragmites communis phototoxicity phragmitis wynn vannella antioxidative phragmites australis abideen qasim rasheed polyphenol phragmites karka monosaccharide phragmitis pollen typhae oceanol limnol phragmitis lishizhen phragmites communis trin semwal bamola rawat phytochem heights golder antioxidative pneumatophores mangrove avicennia sonneratia apetala rosiglitazone phragmitis jilin nahid mazumder hepato methanolic syzygium cumini skeels hepatoprotective antihepatic phragmitis phragmitis smads phragmitis xiu notoginseng chuanxiong ferelli hydrating moisturizer phragmites communis melanogenesis b16f10 biopha chictr1900023052 phragmitis myelotoxicity phragmitis taishan oladipo iku ntwasa aupt bimetallic phragmites australis phragmitis phragmitis phragmitis phragmitis phragmitis husb 11655_2022_3572_moesm1_esm phragmitis 11655_2022_3572_moesm2_esm phragmitis 11655_2022_3572_moesm3_esm phragmitis','Abstract Rhizoma phragmitis is a common Chinese herbal medicine whose effects are defined as ‘clearing heat and fire, promoting fluid production to quench thirst, eliminating irritability, stopping vomiting, and disinhibiting urine’. During the Novel Coronavirus epidemic in 2020, the Weijing Decoction and Wuye Lugen Decoction, with Rhizoma phragmitis as the main herbal component, were included in The Pneumonia Treatment Protocol for Novel Coronavirus Infection (Trial Version 5) due to remarkable antiviral effects. Modern pharmacological studies have shown that Rhizoma phragmitis has antiviral, antioxidative, anti-inflammatory, analgesic, and hypoglycemic functions, lowers blood lipids and protects the liver and kidney. This review aims to provide a systematic summary of the botany, traditional applications, phytochemistry, pharmacology and toxicology of Rhizoma phragmitis . Electronic Supplementary Material Supplementary material (Appendixes 1–3) is available in the online version of this article at 10.1007/s11655-022-3572-1. Keywords: Rhizoma phragmitis , pharmacology, phytochemistry, Chinese medicine Electronic supplementary material 11655_2022_3572_MOESM1_ESM.pdf (35.1KB, pdf) Appendix 1. Details of Prescriptions Containing Rhizoma phragmitis 11655_2022_3572_MOESM2_ESM.pdf (171.2KB, pdf) Appendix 2. Main Components of Rhizoma phragmitis 11655_2022_3572_MOESM3_ESM.pdf (89.5KB, pdf) Appendix 3. Pharmacological Activities of Rhizome phragmitis Author Contributions Ren Y drafted the manuscript. Cui GD was responsible for the literature screening and data extraction of this paper. Yao H and Zi CY were responsible for proofreading of the article. Gao YX and He LS revised and commented on the manuscript. All authors have read and approved the final version for publication. Conflict of Interest All the authors declare that there is no conflict of interest regarding the publication of this paper. References 1. Sauvêtre A, Schröder P. Uptake of carbamazepine by rhizomes and endophytic bacteria of Phragmites australis. Front Plant Sci. 2015;6:83. doi: 10.3389/fpls.2015.00083. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 2. He Y, Langenhoff AAM, Sutton NB, et al. Metabolism of ibuprofen by Phragmites australis: uptake and phytodegradation. Environ Sci Technol. 2017;51:4576–4584. doi: 10.1021/acs.est.7b00458. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 3. Schröder P, Maier H, Debus R. Detoxification of herbicides in Phragmites australis. Z Naturforsch C J Biosci. 2005;60:317–324. doi: 10.1515/znc-2005-3-417. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 4. Park SJ, Kim YW, Park MK, et al. Anti-inflammatory steroid from Phragmitis Rhizoma modulates LPS-mediated signaling through inhibition of NF-κB pathway. Inflammation. 2016;39:727–734. doi: 10.1007/s10753-015-0299-6. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] 5. Chen YH, Liu XC, Jiang ZP, et al. Determination of p-coumaric acid in the extract of Rhizoma phragmitis from different areas. Mod Food (Chin) 2021:196–198,201. 6. Wang ZH, Guo QM, Zhou FQ. Progress in chemical composition pharmacological functions development and utilization of Phragmites australis. J Liaoning Univ Tradit Chin Med (Chin) 2014;16:81–83. [ Google Scholar ] 7. da Co