INSERT INTO corpus VALUES(4703,'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1566727','Somatic and heritable effects of environmental genotoxins and the emergence of evolutionary toxicology.','Bickham JW, Smolen MJ.','1994','inbreeding polluted bickham hanks slider turtles pseudemys scripta contam bf01061989 bickham sawin mcbee triethylenemelamine cyto bickham sawin mcbee derr triethylenemelamine cyto cann stoneking 325031a0 dieter newbold sugino intraspecific bickham slider turtles trachemys scripta inhabiting contam bf01065340 lyne bickham tb00688 mcbee bickham peromyscus leucopus sigmodon hispidus petrochemical karyology contam bf01055418 mcbee bickham petrochemical contam bf01689090 shugart halbrook tb00687','Abstract The genetic effects of environmental pollutants include mutations in somatic cells or germinal cells that are the direct result of exposure to toxicants. Biomarkers that detect such mutagenic effects have been developed and tested in field studies on wildlife populations. However, another class of genetic effects resulting from pollution exposure exists. Specifically, changes in allele frequencies of populations will occur as a result of population bottlenecks, inbreeding, or selection at loci critical for survival in polluted environments. We describe how such genetic alterations can be studied at the population level using the techniques of molecular genetics, and we predict the development of a new field, evolutionary toxicology, that will address such issues. Full text PDF Previous 25 26 27 28 Next Selected References These references are in PubMed. This may not be the complete list of references from this article. Bickham J. W., Hanks B. G., Smolen M. J., Lamb T., Gibbons J. W. Flow cytometric analysis of the effects of low-level radiation exposure on natural populations of slider turtles (Pseudemys scripta). Arch Environ Contam Toxicol. 1988 Nov;17(6):837–841. doi: 10.1007/BF01061989. [ DOI ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ] Bickham J. W., Sawin V. 