INSERT INTO corpus VALUES(4732,'https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC1437487','Clinical pharmacology and general patient care in two teaching hospitals.','Wood SM, Turner P, Vere D.','1980','rawlins','Abstract The clinical responsibilities and activities over 12-month periods of the Departments of Clinical Pharmacology of two London teaching hospitals have been analysed. The results suggest that clinical pharmacology should not be regarded only as an academic specialty but that it has an important role in patient care. Full text PDF Previous 355 356 357 358 Next Selected References These references are in PubMed. This may not be the complete list of references from this article. Rawlins M. D. Clinical pharmacology in the National Health Service. J R Soc Med. 1978 Aug;71(8):556–557. doi: 10.1177/014107687807100802. [ DOI ] [ PMC free article ] [ PubMed ] [ Google Scholar ]',5,'2025-10-15 10:10:41','2025-10-15 10:10:41');
